# The payload must be stored and served BYTE-FOR-BYTE as it sits on disk.
#
# The launcher verifies every download against a SHA-256 in manifest.json. Git's
# line-ending normalisation (core.autocrlf=true on Windows) silently rewrites CRLF
# to LF on commit, which changes the bytes GitHub serves and makes every text file
# fail its hash check. Marking the payload as binary disables all conversion.
#
# Do not remove this. tools/check-published.ps1 exists to catch it if you do.
payload/** -text -diff

# Repo sources are normal text and may be normalised freely.
*.ps1   text
*.cs    text
*.md    text
